 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 508237,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Write the inequality shown by the graph with the boundary line <span data-math=\"y = -2x + 3\">y = -2x + 3</span>.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/c1ea5c7500b5fd4b.jpg\" alt=\"A line is plotted on an x y coordinate plane. The x and y axes range from negative 8 to 8, in increments of 1. The line passes through the following points, (negative 2, 7), (0, 3), (1.5, 0), and (5, negative 7). The region to the right of the line is shaded. Note: all values are approximate.\">",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The boundary line for this graph is given: <span data-math=\"y =  - 2x + 3\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Test a point not on the line to see if <span data-math=\"y \\ge  - 2x + 3\"></span> is the answer:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(0, 0)\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0 \\ge  - 2\\left( 0 \\right) + 3\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0 \\ge 3\"></span> is not true, so <span data-math=\"(0, 0)\"></span> is not a solution. That is good, since the proposed solution is the points above the given line.</p>\n<p>Test <span data-math=\"(5,1)\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"1 \\ge  - 2\\left( 5 \\right) + 3\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"1 \\ge -10 + 3\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"1 \\ge -7\"></span> is true, so shading above the line is correct.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y \\ge - 2x + 3\"></span> is the answer.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"y \\geq  - 2x + 3\">y \\geq  - 2x + 3</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
